                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I’m not sure how you ended up with this game. In my case, it just appeared in my library one day. I’m pretty sure it was a reward for earning badges in another game—or something like that—though it could just as easily have come from some obscure bundle\r\n\r\nThat said, since you can pick it up for as little as 50 cents, there’s really no reason not to. It’s an experience that lasts about an hour and a half; the minimalist mechanic—connecting squares—gradually ramps up in difficulty, reaching a sweet spot that’s engaging without becoming overly frustrating\r\n\r\nThe developer has other similar games, all in the same price range. It’s not a bad idea to check them out if you’re looking for a quick, bite-sized experience—kind of like buying a newspaper just for the Sudoku",
